This is a default "all rights reserved" notice added so the release pipeline has
a LICENSE file to bundle. It grants no rights and is NOT a considered license
choice. Before publishing OptionsPilot publicly, replace this file with the
license you actually intend (e.g. MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD-3-Clause, a commercial
EULA, or a deliberate proprietary "all rights reserved"). The release packaging
(scripts/package_release.ps1) bundles whatever this file contains verbatim.

Note also that the app vendors a third-party charting library under Apache-2.0
(optionspilot/ui/static/lightweight-charts.js) whose own license terms continue
to apply regardless of the license chosen for OptionsPilot itself.
